From: Datadog Agent Build <agent-build@datadoghq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] link -lm -ldl -lrt only when needed

The default_link_flags feature adds -lm -ldl -lrt to every link. On glibc
older than 2.34 these libraries are separate, so every binary gets
libm.so.6, libdl.so.2 and librt.so.1 as DT_NEEDED even when it uses none
of their symbols. Wrap them in --as-needed.

---
--- a/toolchain/cc_toolchain_config.bzl
+++ b/toolchain/cc_toolchain_config.bzl
@@ -123,9 +123,11 @@
                         flags = [
                             "-Wl,-z,relro,-z,now",
                             "-pass-exit-codes",
+                            "-Wl,--push-state,-as-needed",
                             "-lm",
                             "-ldl",
                             "-lrt",
+                            "-Wl,--pop-state",
                             "-pthread",
                         ],
                     ),
